{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/700580-how-would-a-demon-acquire-a-true-soul","id":700580,"title":"How would a Demon acquire a true soul?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-14T02:46:56-07:00","id":700580,"title":"How would a Demon acquire a true soul?","content":"Let's suppose a Demon finds out that his Primum cannot pass onto an afterlife like a true soul can. Maybe it was a Mage who told him this after looking for the Demon's Oneiros and finding that there are only Oneiroi associated with the Covers, and sub-par ones at that. What could the Demon do to alter its Primum into something that works like a true soul? Prometheans can turn their Azoth into a soul when they complete the Great Work, so perhaps the Divine Fire/Principle could do the same for Demons, and even other splats with abnormal souls (e.g. changelings and mummies). Archmages with enough dots in the right Arcana could cast an Excision spell to remove the Demon's template, at the risk of displeasing the God-Machine (if it is indeed a patron of Demons in the Pax Arcana). The Demon could try his luck at becoming an Integrator and convincing the God-Machine to modify him. Perhaps a completed Cipher could show the way, but I'm not sure if Ciphers can do that. Beyond these options, I don't know what the Demon could do. Any suggestions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 10-14-2015, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T03:21:38-07:00","id":700610,"title":"","content":"For all intents and purposes, the Demon <i>is</i> a soul, but if you want to do something different, it'd have to be story-level. Prometheans have a long march towards this very end, and Mummies have to wrestle their souls from the hands of the Judges themselves (metaphorically, of course. Very few of the Judges actually have hands).<br /> <br /> I'd rule that, at the very least, the Demon in question would have to have very high, if not maxed, Primum and access to a suborned Recycling Facility with which to edit themselves a soul. This should also count as a massive break in cover - &quot;Going Loud&quot; massive. <br /> <br /> I'm imagining some huge, climactic scene: here are Hunter Angels all over you, there's Aether in the air, you've lost your Cover and the messing around you did with that reclamation Infrastructure is causing some really weird physics to happen around here. Can you get out with your newly-forged soul intact? Well, we're out of time, so I suppose we find out next session.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, and, while I'm not familiar enough with Mage to know what the Pax Arcana is, I can pretty much guarantee you that the God-Machine is not the Demon's &quot;patron.&quot; Certainly of Angels, but Demons are explicitly disconnected from the God-Machine- it's what makes them Demons, and, while he works in mysterious ways, I'm quite sure the Machine would be quite happy to have some of those little pests running around without powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T06:34:32-07:00","id":700754,"title":"","content":"There is the theory that angels can fall because the God-Machine wants them to, so it is possible that the G-M is the Demon's pax patron. <br /> <br /> This being the word of darkness, the easiest way to get a soul would be to take it from someone else. A mage can help. An infernal demon could probably help. The God-Machine probably has a soul removal-omatic somewhere as infrastructure. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T06:38:03-07:00","id":700756,"title":"","content":"How would a Demon acquire a soul? &quot;Just sign on the dotted line.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The real question is: why would a Demon be interested in such a thing? They can pretty much exist indefinitely. And such an afterlife sounds an awful lot like the Hell some demon's seek anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T06:43:14-07:00","id":700757,"title":"","content":"As has been brought up, Demons are physically their souls. Their demonic form is flesh and spirit for them both.<br /> <br /> So a demon wanting to go to some afterlife is going to have to figure out the metaphysics of that afterlife, hack into the systems of it, bind the demonic form to a cover in such a way that appeases those systems, and then die and hope that everything they did hooks and that their choice of Hell can overlook the fine details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T07:28:13-07:00","id":700785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrBreaksIt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/700580-how-would-a-demon-acquire-a-true-soul?p=700610#post700610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and, while I'm not familiar enough with Mage to know what the Pax Arcana is, I can pretty much guarantee you that the God-Machine is not the Demon's &quot;patron.&quot; Certainly of Angels, but Demons are explicitly disconnected from the God-Machine- it's what makes them Demons, and, while he works in mysterious ways, I'm quite sure the Machine would be quite happy to have some of those little pests running around without powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>The biggest reason for the Machine's pursuit of the Unchained is because <i>they are significant investments of Its resources that have run off with themselves and collected information on obscure parts of It</i>, which is pretty much all the reason it needs to intervene in outside attempts to subvert those resources from above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T07:32:34-07:00","id":700786,"title":"","content":"It's like if your elbow decided to just run off. You might be mad as hell at your elbow, but you also kind of need it to operate normally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T07:50:19-07:00","id":700808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/700580-how-would-a-demon-acquire-a-true-soul?p=700786#post700786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's like if your elbow decided to just run off. You might be mad as hell at your elbow, but you also kind of need it to operate normally.</div> </div> </div> </div>And also your elbow knows where you put the button that makes your leg fall off. You don't want your elbow using that knowledge, but you <i>definitely</i> don't want that information in the hands of your terrible neighbor Winona.<br /> <br /> \u2026This analogy went to weird places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T08:20:15-07:00","id":700861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/700580-how-would-a-demon-acquire-a-true-soul?p=700808#post700808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And also your elbow knows where you put the button that makes your leg fall off. You don't want your elbow using that knowledge, but you <i>definitely</i> don't want that information in the hands of your terrible neighbor Winona.<br /> <br /> \u2026This analogy went to weird places.</div> </div> </div> </div>DAMN YOU WINONA!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T09:59:28-07:00","id":701039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/700580-how-would-a-demon-acquire-a-true-soul?p=700808#post700808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And also your elbow knows where you put the button that makes your leg fall off. You don't want your elbow using that knowledge, but you <i>definitely</i> don't want that information in the hands of your terrible neighbor Winona.<br /> <br /> \u2026This analogy went to weird places.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still have no idea why the alley next to Winona's place looks like the Island of the Dolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T11:48:12-07:00","id":701178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/700580-how-would-a-demon-acquire-a-true-soul#post700580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's suppose a Demon finds out that his Primum cannot pass onto an afterlife like a true soul can. Maybe it was a Mage who told him this after looking for the Demon's Oneiros and finding that there are only Oneiroi associated with the Covers, and sub-par ones at that. What could the Demon do to alter its Primum into something that works like a true soul? Prometheans can turn their Azoth into a soul when they complete the Great Work, so perhaps the Divine Fire/Principle could do the same for Demons, and even other splats with abnormal souls (e.g. changelings and mummies). Archmages with enough dots in the right Arcana could cast an Excision spell to remove the Demon's template, at the risking of displeasing the God-Machine (if it is indeed a patron of Demons in the Pax Arcana). The Demon could try his luck at becoming an Integrator and convincing the God-Machine to modify him. Perhaps a completed Cipher could show the way, but I'm not sure if Ciphers can do that. Beyond these options, I don't know what the Demon could do. Any suggestions?</div> </div> </div> </div>As others have said, Demons aren't soulless, they are soul-like. Physical and Ephemeral simultaneously.<br /> <br /> As for getting into the Afterlife...maybe some Cipher build around things like Breach the Gates and Ephemeral Cover. Assuming Breach the Gates won't just let them tear their way in already. But even that won't be exactly like a human passing on, it certain ways it would be better, as the Demon can saunter back into the world whenever it pleases them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T20:47:50-07:00","id":701626,"title":"","content":"There is no more evidence of an Afterlife in NWoD than there is in the real world. That is not to say that there is no afterlife; just that no splat interacts with it. The closest thing is the Underworld, which can be reached with the Breach the Gates Exploit on an Avernian Gate.<br /> <br /> Even the Awakened, (Mages using Soul Magic from the font of reality) don't really know what happens to ghosts that move on, or the Soul after death. The Unchained aren't exactly missing out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T03:41:03-07:00","id":701914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/700580-how-would-a-demon-acquire-a-true-soul#post700580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's suppose a Demon finds out that his Primum cannot pass onto an afterlife like a true soul can.</div> </div> </div> </div> First of all, no one can confirm that. No mage, no Sin-Eater has that knowledge. We don't even know if the afterlife actually exists in the WoD. Mages believe that the &quot;soul&quot; moves on to the Supernal, dumps its experiences, then is reborn, effectively destroying what you were in the first life. This is effectively no different than falling into oblivion, and it should be noted that what the mages consider a &quot;soul&quot; may not be the same thing as a vampire, werewolf, sin-eater, etc would consider a soul. For a Promethean, a &quot;soul&quot; is actually learning to get along with humans, fitting into society and getting rid of the whole Disquiet-inducing uncanny-valley effect of their existance.<br /> <br /> A soul, as per the Soul Loss rules, is nothing more than a spark of personality and willpower that can be removed and interchanged with other souls, serving more as a power core than something more fundamental. When you die (and give up being a ghost), there's no evidence something better comes after.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beyond these options, I don't know what the Demon could do. Any suggestions? </div> </div> </div>That said, lets delve into what would happen if a demon did believe in some kind of happy afterlife, and wanted to go there. The answer is actually a lot simpler than you think. Its called &quot;join the Interrogator Agenda.&quot; Reaching a personal state of enlightenment that you evolve into something more is exactly the kind of thing the Paranoids work at. There is a subset of Interrogator demons that do want to become fully human, get married, have kids, live off the GM radar, and so on.<br /> <br /> How do they do it? Same way everyone else does. Gather information, make plans, break into facilities, develop the Cypher, achieve some form of techno-religious understanding with the universe through bonding with Primum and reaching &quot;Hell.&quot; <br /> <br /> TL;DR - its already part of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T04:02:16-07:00","id":701927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/700580-how-would-a-demon-acquire-a-true-soul?p=701914#post701914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, lets delve into what would happen if a demon did believe in some kind of happy afterlife, and wanted to go there. The answer is actually a lot simpler than you think. Its called &quot;join the Interrogator Agenda.&quot; Reaching a personal state of enlightenment that you evolve into something more is exactly the kind of thing the Paranoids work at. There is a subset of Interrogator demons that do want to become fully human, get married, have kids, live off the GM radar, and so on.<br /> <br /> How do they do it? Same way everyone else does. Gather information, make plans, break into facilities, develop the Cypher, achieve some form of techno-religious understanding with the universe through bonding with Primum and reaching &quot;Hell.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Inquisitor, but yeah. It's one of the things the &quot;gnostic&quot; part of techgnostic is about - the hope and search for a world beyond the God Machine's reach.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T06:08:14-07:00","id":702016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/700580-how-would-a-demon-acquire-a-true-soul?p=701914#post701914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A soul, as per the Soul Loss rules, is nothing more than a spark of personality and willpower that can be removed and interchanged with other souls, serving more as a power core than something more fundamental. When you die (and give up being a ghost), there's no evidence something better comes after.</div> </div> </div> </div> I honestly like to think of it as the &quot;Numinous Self&quot; for precisely this reason. After all,<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Confucius</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...a superior man considers it necessary that the names he uses may be spoken appropriately, and also that what he speaks may be carried out appropriately. What the superior man requires is just that in his words there may be nothing incorrect.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T07:52:02-07:00","id":702087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/700580-how-would-a-demon-acquire-a-true-soul?p=701914#post701914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> First of all, no one can confirm that. No mage, no Sin-Eater has that knowledge. We don't even know if the afterlife actually exists in the WoD. -</div> </div> </div> </div>Well.<br /> <br /> Duat. Probably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T09:55:02-07:00","id":702252,"title":"","content":"Pretty much everyone else has summed up my viewpoint on this matter already, but I may as well throw my two bits in.<br /> <br /> Firstly, demons are already souls as they are, being an inextricable mingling of physical matter and ephemeral matter/energy. They may not have *human* souls, but they do have their own souls.<br /> <br /> Secondly, why would a demon *want* a human soul? As pointed out, apart from maybe Mummies and Duat, there's no concrete evidence as to what, if anything, lies &quot;beyond the veil of death&quot; for humans and other humanoids. The confirmable alternate planes of existence can already be accessed through Breach the Gates. It's kind of like having the executive keys and then taking on a job as a janitor so that you can get into all the different bathrooms.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, really, unless I'm drastically misremembering the corebook, demons don't want to be human to that extent. In fact, given demons exist under the maxim that a &quot;soul&quot; is nothing more than a cosmic bank account and the sum of one's debits and credits, which is why invoking a Soul Pact extinguishes the former human's soul and leaves a hole in existence that the demon can then occupy, it makes sense that demons would consider a &quot;human soul&quot; to be a step *down* from their innate existence.<br /> <br /> Demons want to be free of the God-Machine, and the right to indulge themselves in pleasures humans don't even realise they have. The right to make their own decisions, the right to think and feel as they want. They don't want to physically and mentally *be* humans. Demons aren't Prometheans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T05:16:12-07:00","id":703231,"title":"","content":"An Integrator following the true divinity movement could well be interested in such a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T06:29:33-07:00","id":703329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/700580-how-would-a-demon-acquire-a-true-soul?p=702252#post702252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly, why would a demon *want* a human soul?</div> </div> </div> </div> Generalities tend to not be true for everyone. There are always exceptions. Especially Guardians, who fall for love, and may want to grow old and die with their beloved families. All you need is one, and that one can easily be a PC. Or are you saying that a PC can't have that as an aspiration?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Demons want to be free of the God-Machine, and the right to indulge themselves in pleasures humans don't even realise they have. </div> </div> </div> Tempters certainly do. However, you cannot say the same thing of the other three Agendas nor the Uncalled. A significant number of Sabatours often fight the God Machine out of hate, not desire for freedom. Inquisitors aren't known for indulging in pleasure. Integrators? Don't want to be free, they want to be angels with their memories and mind intact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Demons aren't Prometheans. </div> </div> </div>Vampires aren't Prometheans, and yet we still have Golconda as a thing. There are werewolves who hate being Uratha and want to become human again. Just because its not the focus of the game doesn't mean you can't have individuals who are interested in such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T06:33:22-07:00","id":703331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/700580-how-would-a-demon-acquire-a-true-soul?p=703329#post703329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires aren't Prometheans, and yet we still have Golconda as a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a Grandfather Clause thing. Vampires have had Golconda for longer than the Promethean line has <i>existed. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T08:03:20-07:00","id":703468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/700580-how-would-a-demon-acquire-a-true-soul?p=703331#post703331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a Grandfather Clause thing. Vampires have had Golconda for longer than the Promethean line has <i>existed. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>Its a &quot;this shows up in nearly half of vampire stories in existance!&quot; thing. Its a common vampire trope, just like it is for other supernaturals, and there are instances throughout the Requiem line of the becoming-human thing that is unrelated to Golconda. Claiming the concept is only grandfathered in does disservice to the vast amount of lore both in game and in popular culture on the subject.<br /> <br /> Giving up Heaven's blessings, even all divine power, to live among mortal families is a theme appropriate for demons. Its also part of Descent's lore. It happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T14:52:40-07:00","id":703828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/700580-how-would-a-demon-acquire-a-true-soul?p=703329#post703329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Generalities tend to not be true for everyone. There are always exceptions. Especially Guardians, who fall for love, and may want to grow old and die with their beloved families. All you need is one, and that one can easily be a PC. Or are you saying that a PC can't have that as an aspiration?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, thing is, growing old and dying with your loved ones? That's already written into the game. You just stay in cover. If a demon's cover dies of old age? The demon goes with it. Demons have to <b>work</b> to be immortal, mostly by constantly switching to new covers. This is stated <i>in the corebook</i>. Being a demon doesn't mean you can't die with your human loved ones if you think that's preferable to going on. And, as said above, there's no proof of any sort of special afterlife in-universe.<br /> <br /> People who die of old age generally <i>don't leave ghosts</i>. There's nothing to really convince a demon they need to seek something more than just adhering to their Cover.<br /> <br /> Remember, a Cover is only a skin-suit <i>if the demon thinks of it that way</i>. Many, <b>many</b> demons establish one Cover that is &quot;just for me&quot;. To them, it <b>is</b> their identity, as much who they are as the flickering abomination of transdimensional algorithms and eldritch steel that they can choose to appear as. When you consciously exist on the quantum level, identity isn't an either-or subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T06:11:38-07:00","id":706690,"title":"","content":"Void, you're still speaking in absolutes. You're trying to use a general assumption and apply it to all demons. You want to run the game that way? Go ahead, have fun. You cannot speak for everyone, especially with as many assumptions you are making about how the game works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}